course: dictionary
lesson: 7876
title: A king called raja
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A raja is a king or prince in India and other parts of South and Southeast Asia, long ago. You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around it, because they are its context. «Raja Moyang Kaban, King of the Elephants, gets muddy legs.» The words after the name tell you what a raja is: a king.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Raja Abdullah, King of the Crocodiles, gets a mouthful of salt water.» If you swap raja for king, the sentence still makes sense: King Abdullah, King of the Crocodiles. So raja means king.
explain: Raja is also used as a title of honour for an Indian ruler or nobleman. Some words are related to it. Maharaja means great king, and rani means a raja's wife or a queen. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A raja is a king or prince in India, or in other parts of South and Southeast Asia, in the past.
fact: Raja can also be a title of honour for an Indian ruler or nobleman.
fact: «Maharaja» means great king, and «rani» means a raja's wife or a queen.
fact: The word «raja» comes from the Sanskrit word «rājan», which means king.
fact: In history lessons, rajas ruled many small Indian states under the British. Stories often show rajas in palaces with elephants and jewels, but these pictures are often made up or exaggerated.
exercise: «Raja Abdullah, King of the Crocodiles, gets a mouthful of salt water.» What does raja mean here? | *King | Fisherman | Sea | Crocodile
exercise: Rani is a word you may meet with raja. What does rani mean? | A small fish | A beach with bare sand | A kind of elephant | *A raja's wife or a queen
exercise: What does maharaja mean? | *Great king | Small fish | Sea monster | Muddy legs
test: Which words in this sentence help you work out what raja means? «Raja Moyang Kaban, King of the Elephants, gets muddy legs.* | Beaches are left bare | Little fish die | Muddy legs | *King of the Elephants
test: Are the pictures of rajas in old adventure books always true? | Yes, every raja lived in a palace with elephants | Yes, rajas had no palaces at all | Yes, rajas never wore any jewels | *No, they are often made up or exaggerated
exam: Which word means a raja's wife or a queen? | Raj | *Rani | Maharaja | Dinnae
